These errors are very easy to fix.
Here is exactly what happened:
 1. **Expected 2 arguments but found 3**: We updated the backend service method initiateValidation to take the entire MultipartFile object directly (so it can check the file size), but your controller was still trying to pass the old 3 arguments (InputStream, filename, postingDate).
 2. **sMaxAge error**: You are using a newer version of Spring Boot (v3+). In newer versions, the CacheControl class requires a java.time.Duration object instead of a raw integer 0.
 3. **Duplicate Returns**: In your downloadBatchExcel method, you had two return ResponseEntity... statements at the bottom, which causes an "unreachable code" compilation error.
Here are the exact, cleaned-up replacements for both methods in your **VoucherPostingController.java**.
### 1. Replace the initiateValidation Method
Find your initiateValidation method (around line 118) and replace it entirely with this. Notice how it now passes file directly and uses Duration.ZERO for the cache headers.
```java
    @PostMapping(value = "/bulk-validate-init", consumes = MediaType.MULTIPART_FORM_DATA_VALUE)
    public ResponseEntity<Map<String, Object>> initiateValidation(
            @RequestParam("file") MultipartFile file,
            @RequestParam("postingDate") @DateTimeFormat(pattern = "dd/MM/yyyy") LocalDate postingDate,
            HttpServletRequest request) {

        if (file == null || file.isEmpty()) {
            throw new CustomExceptions.FileProcessingException("File is missing or empty");
        }

        try {
            log.info("VALIDATION_INIT | File: {} | Date: {}", file.getOriginalFilename(), postingDate);

            // FIX 1: Pass the MultipartFile directly (Matches the new 2-argument signature)
            String reqId = voucherBulkValidationService.initiateValidation(file, postingDate);

            // Build Security Headers for Upload
            HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
            // FIX 2: Use java.time.Duration.ZERO for Spring Boot 3+ compatibility
            headers.setCacheControl(org.springframework.http.CacheControl.noCache().mustRevalidate().sMaxAge(java.time.Duration.ZERO));
            headers.setPragma("no-cache");
            headers.setExpires(0L);
            headers.set("X-Content-Type-Options", "nosniff");
            headers.set("Content-Security-Policy", "default-src 'self'");

            // Return 200 OK with the security headers attached
            return ResponseEntity.ok()
                    .headers(headers)
                    .body(Map.of("status", "QUEUED", "requestId", reqId));

        } catch (IOException e) {
            log.error("VALIDATION_IO_FAIL | File: {}", file.getOriginalFilename());
            throw new CustomExceptions.FileProcessingException("Failed to read uploaded file.");
        }
    }

```
### 2. Replace the downloadBatchExcel Method
Find your downloadBatchExcel method (around line 230). Replace it completely with this clean version to resolve the duplicate return statements and attach the security headers correctly.
```java
    @GetMapping("/download-batch/{batchId}")
    public ResponseEntity<byte[]> downloadBatchExcel(@PathVariable String batchId) {
        
        // 1. Get the byte array from your service
        byte[] fileData = voucherRequestService.generateBatchExcel(batchId);

        // 2. Build Security Headers
        HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
        // Use java.time.Duration.ZERO for Spring Boot 3+ compatibility
        headers.setCacheControl(org.springframework.http.CacheControl.noCache().mustRevalidate().sMaxAge(java.time.Duration.ZERO));
        headers.setPragma("no-cache");
        headers.setExpires(0L);
        headers.set("X-Content-Type-Options", "nosniff");
        headers.set("Content-Security-Policy", "default-src 'self'");
        
        // Attachment and MIME Type Headers
        headers.set(HttpHeaders.CONTENT_DISPOSITION, "attachment; filename=\"Batch_" + batchId + ".xlsx\"");
        headers.set(HttpHeaders.CONTENT_TYPE, "application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet");

        // 3. Return the response strictly once
        return ResponseEntity.ok()
                .headers(headers)
                .body(fileData);
    }

